{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for exact c6ef8a4e35febc65c2fa250505a4dad1101bb12b, all25 assigned artifacts, primary6c0674a43db636340a4dae61c7122249d7092b4a first. Nine P2 source defects remain.\n\n1. Concurrent creation can change the original bearer. hosted.ts282–347 checks state before awaiting custody, entry and standing, then unconditionally mints and overwrites the answer. A second same-op retry while the first awaits standing can return a different bearer; one successful caller gets an invalid credential. Custody releases its lock before those awaits. Recheck/serialize the durable terminal transition and return the original answer; witness the concurrent handoff.\n\n2. Expired answer bodies remain in storage. hosted.ts139–144 returns stale without clearing control.answer; agent.answer also retains the plaintext creation bearer. Remove expired bodies from both copies after the original deadline plus seven days, preserving fingerprints, deadlines, tombstones and unfinished reservations. Verify actual persisted rows, not merely a409 response.\n\n3. A completed control replay has new effects. hosted.ts369–390 returns a historical200 then closes the current HTTP layer. Rotate, open a new legacy stream, then replay that op: the newer stream closes although no new rotation occurred. Close only streams invalidated by a newly committed action; retained replay must return its original outcome without disturbing later sessions.\n\n4. Unfinished enrollment cannot be retired. hosted.ts357–358 rejects enrolling before authority checks. Native enrol may already be accepted while readback/standing remains unavailable, leaving even an admin unable to retire the hosted object. Permit authorized retirement and prevent an in-flight create from resurrecting it. Native key revocation remains separately required.\n\n5. Archived refusals cannot complete repeated archival. sqlite-custody.ts148 inserts into archive without conflict handling; write187–201 recreates a live identity while its archive copy remains. Custody.send302–320 permits explicit refused resubmission. When that identity becomes due for archival again, the duplicate primary key rolls back terminal publication. Give reactivation and re-archival coherent atomic ownership while preserving history; witness archived refusal through retry, terminal result, re-archive and replay.\n\n6. Completion reservations are renewed at the wrong boundary. sqlite-custody.ts119–128 reserves the full constant rather than net growth, and185 re-arms every nonterminal result write. At a saturated budget, a65th lost outcome spills a row, consumes reservation, then its unknown-record write demands fresh capacity after dispatch although the held capacity covers completion. Ordinary terminal-act steps have the opposite defect: custody.ts394–397 leaves act phase terminal, so write skips arm before dispatch. Reserve at dispatch boundaries and consume covered results; witness full-budget completion, repeated terminal-act steps and storage failure. Segment rows/index are atomic together; interrupted-prefix trimming is an existing port behavior, not a separate wholesale-history-loss finding.\n\n7. Modern listens do not close gracefully. http.ts267–277,289–292 and wire.ts305–308 discard listeners/counts without completing their SSE bodies. Bearer/retire leaves an acknowledged July response hanging without final event or EOF. Retain close callbacks and distinguish graceful from abrupt ending; witness both revisions with streams open.\n\n8. Concurrent legacy GETs exceed the four-stream limit. http.ts240–254 checks capacity before awaited snapshot and adds afterward. With three streams, two concurrent GETs on different sessions can both enter and create five; node.ts374–379 permits this concurrency. Reserve or recheck capacity atomically, including cancellation/session-ending races; witness blocked-snapshot concurrent admission.\n\n9. Control body limits apply after full buffering. worker.ts489–494 only shape-parses Control, then arrayBuffer reads the entire unauthenticated body before64KiB enforcement. Bound and cancel the raw stream while reading, retaining exact digest bytes and reporting read failure; witness oversized streaming input never reaching mutation.\n\nArchitecture: the shared HTTP layer, native enrollment/current-authority ports and durable custody approach fit the adopted design, but lifecycle and reservation failures prevent approval. Security: preserve domain-bound control signatures, original custody and native revocation; repair secret retention, pre-auth resource bounds and credential/stream lifecycle. Simplification: centralize bounded byte reading, atomic terminal transitions and reservation ownership rather than adding parallel recovery mechanisms.\n\nAcceptance witnesses must exercise these repairs through the actual Custody and Worker paths. The existing tests omit commissioned concurrent create/reset stages, full-budget and archived-refusal flows, open-stream retirement and portions of H5/H7. Missing tests alone are not counted as extra algorithm defects. Nonblocking: implement/reconcile the adopted256KiB inline threshold; align unsupported-method version errors and request-only JSON-RPC framing with the declared matrix.\n\nCoverage: Root FIRST own logical FULL primary80100 (own0728 FULL prefix71673 exact, all8427 fresh through EOF); Root fresh FULL hosted29593/sqlite15830/bytes-session3482/contract-session6682, docs-mcp U3 FULL9013 and complete selected design, custody, HTTP/wire/Node/Worker units. Four independent disjoint reports FULL-read by Root; their body coverage is theirs, not borrowed Root FULL. Other large bodies remain Root PARTIAL; generated modules/lockfile are opaque to semantic review. No runtime, test, install, deployment, browser or private gate body was executed/read by Root or reviewers. Owner gate assertions remain owner evidence; original failures stay retained. Deployment/live checks, export and Start parity remain owed. New candidate must preserve incoming deliveries and use normal exact-head review; no force or stale-tree replacement.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6c0674a43db636340a4dae61c7122249d7092b4a","binding":"assigned","head":"c6ef8a4e35febc65c2fa250505a4dad1101bb12b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5f9f2e4d9570d47af410dd363e9a6ce8721d4d43\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f948d60ae6641c510f0dcc17517f6dabf0a3e367\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ea6f5b86c1395c0174f9317ef3d1bda1cea406e5\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:478a00cfa0a237c032d5543dde4ea928118c7466\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a31b2e1632438998eadc9971f7beea2988f24ba7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}